  "generated_text": "To determine if $f(x) = \\frac{5^x - 1}{5^x + 1}$ is even, odd, or neither, we need to evaluate $f(-x)$ and compare it to $f(x)$.\n\n1. Calculate $f(-x)$:\n   \\[\n   f(-x) = \\frac{5^{-x} - 1}{5^{-x} + 1}\n   \\]\n   Since $5^{-x} = \\frac{1}{5^x}$, we can rewrite $f(-x)$ as:\n   \\[\n   f(-x) = \\frac{\\frac{1}{5^x} - 1}{\\frac{1}{5^x} + 1}\n   \\]\n\n2. Compare $f(-x)$ to $f(x)$:\n   \\[\n   f(-x) = \\frac{1 - 5^x}{5^x + 1} = -f(x)\n   \\]\n   Since $f(-x) = -f(x)$, we conclude that $f(x)$ is an odd function.\n\nConclusion:\nThe function $f(x)$ is odd, so the answer is $\\boxed{\\text{odd}}$.",
